      "id": "claim_eb29ea2ba7ff40f2b60f1a64ab55325b",
      "statement": "The production Dockerfile is a two-stage build on node:22-bookworm-slim: the builder stage copies all workspace manifests for layer caching, runs npm ci, copies workspace src trees, and runs npm run build; the runner stage installs production deps only (npm ci --omit=dev), copies dist/ for shared, server, dashboard, telegram, agent-catalog, and mcp-server (plus agent-catalog's runtime schema files and the corpus/negative-evidence data files), and starts packages/server/dist/index.js via docker-entrypoint.sh; ransomware-module dist is not copied into the production image.",
